id: pm-extension-scalar-validation
title: Validate contributed scalar flag values before extension handler dispatch
description: "A harmless echo fixture declares type bool but --enabled not-a-boolean reaches its handler as a string. Coercion preserves invalid input for later validation, yet current dynamic dispatch validates only allowed/required/disabled option keys. Establish an explicit compatible scalar-validation contract for extension authors."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T16:21:40.172Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T14:04:28.855Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-16T14:04:28.036Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-16T14:04:28.036Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Define compatibility for invalid number/boolean tokens and optional no-value presence; Apply shared SDK-owned scalar validation before handler invocation where opted in or required by the supported contract; Preserve canonical switch positional behavior and legacy bool grammar; Independently assert malformed value refusals and valid coercion/default/list cases through public CLI/SDK
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "FlagDefinition.value_validation (coerce default, strict) declared in extension-types, validated at registration (unknown policy and strict on string/untyped flags refused), and enforced before dispatch in the loose option coercer: malformed number/boolean tokens refuse with extension_flag_value_invalid naming flag, command, expected grammar and received token; list entries validated individually; switch presence, --no- negation, the legacy bool optional-value grammar and defaults preserved. Shared helper describeFlagScalarValueFailure exported through runtime-primitives. Attached boolean list switches are validated before presence coercion, splitting CSV tokens while preserving repeatable occurrences, valid literals, alias ordering and positional presence."
expected_result: "Extension authors can declare scalar validation that rejects malformed boolean and numeric inputs before dispatch while preserving valid aliases, defaults, optional presence and list ordering across public SDK and CLI."
actual_result: "10540 tests pass with three skips and exact source coverage: 69207/69207 statements, 53134/53134 branches, 14251/14251 functions and 65701/65701 lines. The scalar/loader/CLI linked command passes 137 cases and the SDK/CLI/MCP command passes 87. Three filtered regressions fail on isolated unchanged 53aa49473. Nine packed npx/bunx workflows, four typecheck projects, focused lint, docs links and generated contract/error/capability/SDK surface checks pass. Final-head hosted checks and full review remain required."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-gh1466,discovered_from,"2026-10-14T16:47:25.265Z","harness:codex","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T16:21:40.172Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict2965-item all-status corpus; focused live extension invalid scalar boolean validation search; title/description scan for coercion and scalar-validation owners found only unrelated closed schema-field/numeric-wrapper work. Actual isolated echo reproduction on2026-10-14 returns exit0 and options.enabled=not-a-boolean. This pre-existing issue is separate from pm-gh1466 false preservation and pm-gh1467 optional arity; leave open/unclaimed and do not silently broaden those compatibility fixes."
  "2026-10-14T16:47:27.101Z","harness:codex","Discovery provenance: the malformed scalar echo was encountered while implementing pm-gh1466, so record discovered_from rather than a fabricated ordering/recurrence relationship. Risk, confidence, estimate and expected outcome are now complete. This separately queued enhancement remains open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-15T12:29:34.130Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation note (2026-10-15): FlagDefinition gains value_validation (\"coerce\" | \"strict\"). The default stays the historical passthrough (compatible). strict refuses malformed number/boolean tokens before the extension handler runs with extension_flag_value_invalid (exit 2), naming flag, command path, expected grammar and received token; list entries are checked one by one; a value-less number flag is \"received no value\". Canonical switch presence and the legacy bool optional-value grammar are preserved: a switch followed by a positional resolves to true and keeps the positional in args. Registration refuses an unknown policy and refuses strict on string/untyped flags because there is nothing to validate; the activation failure surfaces in pm package doctor as extension_activate_failed. Shared SDK helper describeFlagScalarValueFailure is exported through runtime-primitives. Verified via a file-based extension fixture in a sandbox and through the public CLI in integration tests.\n"
  "2026-10-15T18:12:24.346Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit): strict scalar validation ran after alias folding, so '--limit 5 -l junk' kept the canonical 5 and silently discarded the malformed alias token. Every supplied spelling of a strict non-list scalar is now validated before mergeAliasOptionKeys discards it; a valid alias still yields to the canonical value. Covered in tests/unit/cli/main-loose-options.spec.ts."
  "2026-10-15T19:01:36.558Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, third pass): two more strict-validation leaks closed. An attached token on a boolean switch (--verbose=maybe) was folded to presence true; the loose tokenizer now marks attached values and a malformed attached token refuses with extension_flag_value_invalid while a following positional keeps presence semantics. An explicitly empty list entry (--ids=, also for repeatable flags) was dropped by list normalization before validation and reached the handler as []; it is now refused before normalization. The coercion loop was split into coerceDefinedLooseOption and helpers to stay under the complexity ceiling, which released one eslint suppression (ceiling 106 to 105)."
  "2026-10-15T19:58:04.047Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit, fourth pass): on a strict CSV list, an empty segment inside one token (--ids=1,,2) was dropped by flattenFlagListValue before validation. refuseEmptyStrictListEntries now splits CSV occurrences on commas before the empty-entry check, while repeatable flags keep commas inside one occurrence so the whole token is reported as the malformed value. Covered in tests/unit/cli/main-loose-options.spec.ts."
  "2026-10-16T11:36:03.631Z","harness:codex","Review evidence correction: the recorded post-fix test-local-mva39gpi-1s1eid ran from 2026-10-15T22:06:32.872Z to 2026-10-15T22:06:44.694Z. Qualify actual_result using its UTC date, 2026-10-15, retaining the rest of the result and the completed implementation status. The prior wording remains in immutable history; this is a metadata correction, not a new test execution."
  "2026-10-16T13:43:07.054Z","harness:codex","Latest full-review remediation: attached boolean-switch values are checked before list presence normalization. CSV lists validate split entries while repeatable lists preserve each occurrence; malformed canonical/alias tokens and empty/CSV-empty entries refuse, while valid true/false/1/0 lists and positional presence retain order and semantics. All 137 linked scalar/loader/public CLI tests pass. Three filtered old-head regressions fail on unchanged 53aa49473; the final full-source run remains required."
  "2026-10-16T14:04:26.988Z","harness:codex","Final local acceptance: 10540 tests pass with three skips and exact source coverage: 69207/69207 statements, 53134/53134 branches, 14251/14251 functions and 65701/65701 lines. The scalar/loader/CLI linked command passes 137 cases and the SDK/CLI/MCP command passes 87. Three filtered regressions fail on isolated unchanged 53aa49473. Nine packed npx/bunx workflows, four typecheck projects, focused lint, docs links and generated contract/error/capability/SDK surface checks pass. Final-head hosted checks and full review remain required."
